Now I show my chocolate.
I hold the chocolate up to the camera.
"Look," I say.
"This is a German brand."
My mother asks: "Is a big supermarket nearby?"
"No," I say.
"My supermarket is closed today."
"It is Sunday."
My brother Diego asks: "Who sells chocolate on a Sunday?"
I laugh.
"A Späti," I answer.
Diego asks: "What is a Späti?"
"It is a small kiosk," I explain.
"It is right around the corner."
"My Späti has everything."
My sister Sofia smiles.
"Enjoy," says my father.
